From 0e2891432028f7f4daf6f25a5ecaff008cba75a9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Pablo Dorado <pablo@bloque.team>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 13:52:18 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(signing): take randomness as a parameter, move OsRng
 to `os-rng`

`signing = ["dep:rand_core", "rand_core/getrandom"]` pulled getrandom
0.2 into every consumer that signs, and getrandom refuses to compile
for targets it does not know. A VOS guest (`riscv64em-vos`) that signs
kernel transfers could not build the crate at all.

`signing` now enables `rand_core` alone. Every function that needs
randomness has a variant that takes the caller's
`R: RngCore + CryptoRng` and is always available with `signing`. The
`OsRng` convenience wrappers keep their names and behaviour behind a
new opt-in feature, `os-rng = ["signing", "rand_core/getrandom"]`;
`helpers` implies it, so its users see no change.

New `*_with_rng` variants: id `random_with_rng`,
`Account::{open,asset,liability}_with_rng`,
`Transfer::builder_with_rng`, `TransferBuilder::new_with_rng`,
`TransferBuilder::{signed_by_with, signed_with_rng,
try_signed_with_rng}`, `proof::signature::sign_with_rng`,
`{SettlementClaim,Voucher,ShieldedVoucher}::sign_with_rng`,
`disclosure::prove_*_with_rng`, `SpendKey::generate_with_rng`,
`EncryptedEnvelope::seal_with_rng`,
`EncryptedNoteEnvelope::{seal_note,seal_note_to_address}_with_rng`.
Existing `Keypair::generate_with`, `CreateAccount::signed_with` and
`Transfer::signed_by_with` already took an RNG and are unchanged.

`TransferBuilder` draws its randomness once, at construction: the
transfer id and a 32-byte seed. Entry ids derive from the seed and the
entry's index, so `debit` / `credit` need no RNG.

Tests that use the `OsRng` wrappers are gated on `os-rng`; the new
`tests/rng_parameter.rs` runs on `signing` alone and drives the kernel
end to end with a seeded RNG.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
