diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
index 3eb835a..119dd2b 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -9,6 +9,42 @@ versions follow [SemVer](https://semver.org/) once we hit 1.0.
 
 ## Unreleased — v0.1.x track
 
+### Changed — randomness is a parameter; `OsRng` moves to `os-rng`
+
+`signing` no longer enables `rand_core/getrandom`, so it builds for
+targets `getrandom` does not support (the VOS guest,
+`riscv64em-vos`; PVM / zkVM guests in general). Every function that
+needs randomness now has a variant that takes the caller's
+`R: RngCore + CryptoRng`, always available with `signing`. The
+`OsRng` convenience wrappers keep their names and behaviour behind a
+new opt-in feature, `os-rng = ["signing", "rand_core/getrandom"]`;
+`helpers` implies it.
+
+| `os-rng` (unchanged name) | Always available with `signing` |
+|---|---|
+| `Keypair::generate` | `Keypair::generate_with` (existing) |
+| `AccountId::random` and every id newtype's `random` | `random_with_rng` |
+| `Account::open` / `asset` / `liability` | `open_with_rng` / `asset_with_rng` / `liability_with_rng` |
+| `CreateAccount::signed` | `CreateAccount::signed_with` (existing) |
+| `Transfer::signed_by` | `Transfer::signed_by_with` (existing) |
+| `Transfer::builder`, `TransferBuilder::new` | `Transfer::builder_with_rng`, `TransferBuilder::new_with_rng` |
+| `TransferBuilder::signed_by` / `signed_with` / `try_signed_with` | `signed_by_with` / `signed_with_rng` / `try_signed_with_rng` |
+| `proof::signature::sign` | `proof::signature::sign_with_rng` |
+| `SettlementClaim::sign`, `Voucher::sign`, `ShieldedVoucher::sign` | `sign_with_rng` |
+| `disclosure::prove_*` | `disclosure::prove_*_with_rng` |
+| `SpendKey::generate` | `SpendKey::generate_with_rng` |
+| `EncryptedEnvelope::seal`, `EncryptedNoteEnvelope::seal_note` / `seal_note_to_address` | `seal_with_rng`, `seal_note_with_rng` / `seal_note_to_address_with_rng` |
+
+`TransferBuilder` now draws its randomness once, at construction: the
+transfer id and a 32-byte seed from which each entry id is derived
+(`blake2b_256("cipher-clerk/transfer-builder/entry-id/v1", seed ||
+index)`, first 16 bytes). Entry ids are still unpredictable and
+unique; `debit` / `credit` no longer need an RNG.
+
+Migration: a consumer that enables `signing` and calls one of the
+`OsRng` wrappers adds `os-rng` to its features. Consumers of
+`helpers` need no change.
+
 ### Changed — `fmd::MAX_PRECISION` 14 → 24
 
 Bumps γ_max to match Penumbra's `decaf377-fmd2::MAX_PRECISION = 24`.
